WEBVTT

00:00:00.482 --> 00:00:05.524
Journey seven: book a meeting. A member requests a meeting time for a

00:00:05.524 --> 00:00:10.493
service with a business. This run takes the journey from ninety-five

00:00:10.493 --> 00:00:11.954
percent to complete.

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:18.059
Until now, every business met at the same five fixed times.

00:00:18.059 --> 00:00:24.199
Now the owner decides. Naomi owns Luzandre.com, and My services has a

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:26.513
new button: Meeting hours.

00:00:27.216 --> 00:00:32.138
The dialog shows the hours in force: the days of the week, from and

00:00:32.138 --> 00:00:36.251
until as Toronto times, and how often a time is offered.

00:00:36.251 --> 00:00:39.336
Requests she already has keep their times.

00:00:40.038 --> 00:00:45.365
Naomi meets on Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday, so she unticks the other

00:00:45.365 --> 00:00:47.166
days and ticks Saturday.

00:00:47.869 --> 00:00:51.966
She sets from to ten, and by mistake until to nine.

00:00:51.966 --> 00:00:57.508
Save hours saves nothing, and the field says: choose a time after ten

00:00:57.508 --> 00:00:57.829
a.m.

00:00:58.531 --> 00:01:04.493
She corrects it to noon and saves. The dialog closes, and My services

00:01:04.493 --> 00:01:06.739
says: meeting hours saved.

00:01:07.449 --> 00:01:12.736
Now a member. Joanna books a meeting with Legacy Financial, a business

00:01:12.736 --> 00:01:17.948
that saved those same hours. She picks a Thursday and is offered four

00:01:17.948 --> 00:01:22.329
times: every thirty minutes from ten, each ending by noon.

00:01:23.031 --> 00:01:28.308
A sixty-minute review must end by noon as well, so eleven thirty is no

00:01:28.308 --> 00:01:29.439
longer offered.

00:01:30.141 --> 00:01:35.640
A Friday is not one of the days. The dialog says Trevor can't meet on

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.589
that day, and names the days he does.

00:01:39.293 --> 00:01:45.536
Joanna goes back to Thursday, chooses ten thirty and sends the request.

00:01:45.536 --> 00:01:50.021
Nothing is charged. Trevor confirms it or declines.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:56.434
Behind the screen, the API decides, and checks again whatever the dialog

00:01:56.434 --> 00:02:01.545
checked. The hours are Toronto times of day on either side of a clock

00:02:01.545 --> 00:02:06.730
change, only the owner sets them, and requests already sent keep their

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:10.804
day, time and status. Nineteen API test cases prove it.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:14.718
Two criteria that had no test now have one.

00:02:14.718 --> 00:02:19.768
In the browser, the note of a booking stops at one thousand characters.

00:02:19.768 --> 00:02:24.676
In the API, the owner gets an in-app notification of the booking, and

00:02:24.676 --> 00:02:27.236
the member one when it is confirmed.

00:02:28.093 --> 00:02:32.993
Requirement two hundred and twenty and decision record forty-seven hold

00:02:32.993 --> 00:02:35.822
this work, and journey seven is complete.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:40.515
Left for the owner: the visual, responsive and accessibility sweeps.

00:02:40.515 --> 00:02:45.415
Different hours on different days, calendars and double booking are not

00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:45.829
built.
